From 6f46b472704aec2533f1410edb47d9477a916d53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:27:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 94/99] dnd: Adds drag and drop of clients, and Window Maker's
 DropCommand.

Clients could not drag and drop: The seat's request_start_drag was not
handled. Drags are now started when requested from a button the client
holds (the pointer grab's serial), and the dragged icon follows the
pointer, above all.

While dragging, the seat has no pointer focus, and surfaces don't pass
the button on: The release goes to the seat after the compositor handled
it, which drops (or cancels) the drag.

As Window Maker's DropCommand, a drag released on a launcher of the Dock,
the Clip or an open drawer, with a `DropCommand`, is taken by the
compositor (`wlmdock` takes no drops): Unless a window is there. It asks
the source for "text/uri-list" (else text), ends the drag as a copy, and
runs the command through `/bin/sh -c`, with "%d" as "$@": The paths of
the dropped files, decoded, as arguments.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
